## Keep source URIs on Studio entity import
================================================================================

Context: Studio Import entity rebased every class, attribute, and relationship
IRI onto the target domain ``base_uri``. Generated OWL then lost the source
identity (``OntologyGenerator._effective_uri`` only emits a stored URI when
the local name matches). Import now copies the source IRI; a rename rewrites
the local name under the source namespace so OWL stays consistent. Name
collisions still skip the copy.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/ontology/EntityImport.py
   Keep source URIs; on rename use ``source_base + new_name``; skip
   relationships by name (``name_exists``); extract class/relationship copy.
2. tests/units/ontology/test_entity_import.py
   Expect source IRIs, rename-under-source-base, empty-URI fallback, OWL
   smoke, and name-based relationship skip.
3. docs/user-guide.md
   Document that imported entities keep source URIs and skip on name collision.
4. docs/advanced_features.md
   Cross-domain import keeps source IRIs instead of rebasing to target
   ``base_uri``.

Modified files:
- src/back/objects/ontology/EntityImport.py
- tests/units/ontology/test_entity_import.py
- docs/user-guide.md
- docs/advanced_features.md
- changelogs/v0.10.0/benoitcayladbx_2026-11-05.log

